Initialization contract checks
==============================

The tests link blueos_infra and pin_init as real GN dependencies. TestAllocator
is registered explicitly by each standalone binary and comes from
//kernel/test_support/allocation. No production module is loaded through a
cross-directory #[path] or include!.

Targets (board="none"):
  ninja -C <out> check_pin_init check_infra_init
  ninja -C <out> check_pin_init_by_miri check_infra_init_by_miri

Use separate output directories for nightly-2024-11-22 and nightly-2026-05-24.
Place the selected toolchain's bin directory directly on PATH before gn gen
and ninja (Cargo build-script probes use a sanitized environment). For Miri,
use nightly-2026-05-24 and set MIRI_SYSROOT before gn gen. Each *_by_miri target
runs both the default model and Tree Borrows, with alloc enabled and std off
in the pin-init runtime library.

check_pin_init verifies macros, stack initialization and the Drop guarantee for
ordinary Box and UnsafeCell. Its compile probes reject MaybeUninit wrapping,
moving a pinned !Unpin value and a PinInit-only initializer on an unpinned field.

check_infra_init covers all four local Box methods, injected allocation failure,
initializer errors, high alignment, zero-sized types, partial field and array
rollback, moving owners, existing uninitialized Boxes, and unwind cleanup.
Opaque tests cover raw access, direct layout, suppressed payload destruction,
and an outer pinned owner's explicit initialization/destruction invariant.
The compile probes reject Opaque's Sync, Unpin and Wrapper implementations and
moving the value returned by the local pin_init method. Each compile suite has
a positive fixture; negative fixtures must produce exactly the specified error
codes with the actual compiled libraries, not a missing dependency diagnostic.

Allocation observations deliberately contain no failing assertions or logging.
black_box prevents the optimizer from removing allocations in observed paths.
Panic tests do not assert counts for allocations made by the panic machinery;
Drop counters and Miri's leak checking verify cleanup instead.

Kernel smoke test: kernel/kernel:run_unittest on qemu_riscv64 and
qemu_mps2_an385 includes pin_init_kernel_allocator_smoke, using KernelAllocator
and the kernel's existing From<AllocError> conversion. Host tests cannot replace
these architecture integration checks.

These checks do not establish safety of all infra containers, external-memory
wrappers, concurrent code or all upstream pin-init APIs. Opaque deliberately has
no automatic payload Drop and no generic Wrapper adapter. TinyArc, intrusive
lists, locks and the future UniqueArc/Arc implementation are outside this work.